1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,212
Out of the box, an AI assistant can only talk.

2
00:00:04,212 --> 00:00:05,632
Tools let it act:

3
00:00:05,632 --> 00:00:09,585
look up an order, search your documentation, list content.

4
00:00:09,585 --> 00:00:14,155
This video shows the built-in tools, who is allowed to use them, and

5
00:00:14,155 --> 00:00:19,220
how you create your own tool instances, without code, from ready-made kinds.

6
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:26,427
A tool is an action the AI can take.

7
00:00:26,427 --> 00:00:30,524
The AI decides by itself when to use one, and you give tools

8
00:00:30,524 --> 00:00:34,310
to an assistant on the Capabilities tab of its profile.

9
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:39,192
Built-in tools come with the Orchard Core AI Agent feature.

10
00:00:39,192 --> 00:00:40,908
They act on the site:

11
00:00:40,908 --> 00:00:45,930
they search and change content, manage features, look up users, and more.

12
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:50,936
Tool instances are tools you set up yourself, such as a lookup in

13
00:00:50,936 --> 00:00:54,473
your order system, or a search of your documentation.

14
00:00:54,473 --> 00:00:58,130
Each one becomes its own tool, with its own permission.

15
00:01:02,321 --> 00:01:05,147
Open the profile and its Capabilities tab.

16
00:01:05,147 --> 00:01:09,327
The Tools section lists the actions the AI can take on this site,

17
00:01:09,327 --> 00:01:14,919
grouped by category, such as Content Management, Features Management or Users Management.

18
00:01:14,919 --> 00:01:18,451
Some only appear when the matching site feature is on.

19
00:01:18,902 --> 00:01:21,385
Search tools finds a tool by name.

20
00:01:21,385 --> 00:01:24,116
Tick a tool to give it to the profile.

21
00:01:24,116 --> 00:01:28,896
Select All Tools ticks every tool, and each category has its own Select

22
00:01:28,896 --> 00:01:30,882
All, but choose with care.

23
00:01:31,333 --> 00:01:32,716
Tools really act.

24
00:01:32,716 --> 00:01:37,409
A profile with Delete Content Item can delete content when someone asks.

25
00:01:37,409 --> 00:01:42,221
Give a public website assistant no tool that changes anything, and give an

26
00:01:42,221 --> 00:01:45,349
admin assistant only the tools its users need.

27
00:01:45,349 --> 00:01:46,673
Then click Save.

28
00:01:50,873 --> 00:01:55,083
Using a profile and using its tools are two separate permissions.

29
00:01:55,083 --> 00:01:58,938
A person can use a tool only when their role has Access any

30
00:01:58,938 --> 00:02:01,963
AI tool, or the permission for that one tool.

31
00:02:02,713 --> 00:02:06,469
A tool that the person may not use is quietly left out, and

32
00:02:06,469 --> 00:02:08,722
the assistant answers without it.

33
00:02:08,722 --> 00:02:12,363
That often looks like a vague answer, or I can't do that.

34
00:02:13,113 --> 00:02:19,145
Access any AI tool is powerful and is given only to administrators by default.

35
00:02:19,145 --> 00:02:22,233
Prefer to grant the individual tools.

36
00:02:26,429 --> 00:02:30,093
Open Access Control, Roles, and edit a role.

37
00:02:30,093 --> 00:02:35,077
In the AI section, Access any AI tool opens every tool, and it

38
00:02:35,077 --> 00:02:37,569
is marked Security Critical.

39
00:02:38,026 --> 00:02:42,528
Below it, each tool has its own permission, Access AI tool and the

40
00:02:42,528 --> 00:02:43,966
name of the tool.

41
00:02:43,966 --> 00:02:49,906
Tick only the tools that role needs, and every tool instance you create appears here too.

42
00:02:54,106 --> 00:02:59,475
Open Artificial Intelligence, Tool Instances, and click Add Tool Instance.

43
00:02:59,475 --> 00:03:03,166
Available Sources lists the kinds you can create:

44
00:03:03,166 --> 00:03:08,870
an HTTP API Request, three kinds of documentation search, and a website search.

45
00:03:08,870 --> 00:03:13,836
A data source search appears when the AI Data Sources feature is on.

46
00:03:14,287 --> 00:03:19,812
Click Add on HTTP API Request, to call a web service such as your order system.

47
00:03:19,812 --> 00:03:24,427
Give it a Name, which the AI turns into the tool's function name,

48
00:03:24,427 --> 00:03:26,767
so it cannot be changed later.

49
00:03:27,223 --> 00:03:31,649
The Description tells the AI what the tool is for and when to use it.

50
00:03:31,649 --> 00:03:36,960
Be specific, for example, looks up the status of a customer's order by order number.

51
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:41,621
When there are several instances of the same kind, the description is the

52
00:03:41,621 --> 00:03:43,923
only way the AI tells them apart.

53
00:03:44,378 --> 00:03:46,921
Fill in the fields of the kind:

54
00:03:46,921 --> 00:03:53,586
the Base URL, the HTTP method, a timeout, and the Authentication type with its credentials.

55
00:03:53,586 --> 00:03:56,404
Your technical team provides these.

56
00:03:56,404 --> 00:04:01,558
A secret such as an API key is stored securely and never shown again.

57
00:04:02,012 --> 00:04:03,112
Click Save.

58
00:04:03,112 --> 00:04:07,962
The instance now appears in the list, ready to be given to a profile.

59
00:04:12,162 --> 00:04:16,588
Open the Capabilities tab of a profile, a profile template or a chat

60
00:04:16,588 --> 00:04:19,159
interaction, and find Tool Instances.

61
00:04:19,159 --> 00:04:21,552
Tick the instance, and click Save.

62
00:04:21,552 --> 00:04:24,422
People also need the permission to use it.

63
00:04:28,622 --> 00:04:33,993
HTTP API Request calls a web service, such as an order or booking system.

64
00:04:33,993 --> 00:04:37,256
Documentation search comes in three kinds:

65
00:04:37,256 --> 00:04:42,762
from a site's sitemap, from a search index file, or from Algolia DocSearch.

66
00:04:43,512 --> 00:04:48,025
Website search uses a site's own live search, such as a WordPress site,

67
00:04:48,025 --> 00:04:50,018
and only needs the Base URL.

68
00:04:50,018 --> 00:04:54,354
Data source search lets the AI search one of your data sources, only

69
00:04:54,354 --> 00:04:55,702
when it needs to.

70
00:04:56,452 --> 00:05:01,152
A data source search cannot force the AI to answer only from your data.

71
00:05:01,152 --> 00:05:05,852
When answers must come from your content, attach the data source on the

72
00:05:05,852 --> 00:05:11,712
Knowledge tab of the profile, and turn on Restrict answers to retrieved data only instead.

73
00:05:12,462 --> 00:05:17,170
With the MCP server feature on, you can also share tools and tool

74
00:05:17,170 --> 00:05:19,623
instances with outside AI apps.

75
00:05:19,623 --> 00:05:25,922
Nothing is shared until you pick it, under Settings, Artificial Intelligence, MCP Server.

76
00:05:30,122 --> 00:05:34,387
A shop gives its assistant an order lookup instance, so customers can ask

77
00:05:34,387 --> 00:05:38,112
where their order is, and the assistant calls the order system.

78
00:05:38,862 --> 00:05:44,017
A software company gives its support assistant a documentation search, so answers come

79
00:05:44,017 --> 00:05:45,922
from the public help center.

80
00:05:46,672 --> 00:05:51,271
An administrator gives an admin assistant only the tools to list content and

81
00:05:51,271 --> 00:05:54,972
check features, and grants those tools to the editors' role.

82
00:05:56,972 --> 00:05:58,924
Tools let an assistant act.

83
00:05:58,924 --> 00:06:03,834
Choose them with care, grant them with the right permissions, and create your

84
00:06:03,834 --> 00:06:06,614
own tool instances from ready-made kinds.

85
00:06:06,614 --> 00:06:08,152
Thanks for watching.

